    "body": "Stack from [ghstack](https://github.com/ezyang/ghstack/tree/0.15.0) (oldest at bottom):\n* #5527\n* __->__ #5526\n* #5136\n* #5525\n\nA replayed CUDA graph runs on whatever streams the driver's graph executor\npicks, so a profile draws one training step across hundreds of single-kernel\nstream lanes. Rank 0 of a Llama3 8B FSDP2 x TP2 GraphTrainer run had 408 GPU\ntracks, 370 of them a single NCCL kernel.\n\nAdd Profiler.Config.cuda_graph_lanes (on by default), which asks torch to\nmove graphed work onto logical lanes: one per process group for collectives,\none per mark_stream stream, and one for everything else. It sets\nCuspyConfig(graph_lanes=\"all\") for Cuspy and passes graph_lanes=\"all\" to\nKineto's export_chrome_trace. Moved events keep the stream they ran on as\noriginal_stream.\n\nBoth need a torch with CuspyConfig.graph_lanes, which landed together with\nprocess group lanes for collectives; on older torch the trace keeps its\nreplay-stream layout, with a warning when it contains CUDA graph work.\n\nWith a prototype of the same lane rule, the same run has 8 GPU tracks on\nCuspy (CUDA graph, mesh_tp, mesh_fsdp, and the eager streams) and 7 on\nKineto. A DeepSeek V3 Dist-MoE FSDP2 x EP2 run has 4.",
